  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"Two volunteers are available at busy return points, and either can handle intake or the lending record.\", \"decision\": \"How should volunteers divide intake and recording work?\", \"goal\": \"Make cup lending and return convenient while keeping the available stock and volunteer work understandable.\", \"problem\": \"A neighborhood café wants to lend reusable cups at community gatherings and recover them afterward. It has a modest cup stock, washable collection crates, a simple lending record, and volunteers who can share short shifts. The plan concerns a small pilot with no deposit or sales system. Different decisions address separate moments in lending, return, and review.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nEach volunteer handles intake and the lending record for a separate stream of guests. A return stays with one person from handover through recording.\nOne volunteer handles cup intake while the other updates the lending record throughout a short block. Each person can concentrate on one part of the return process.\nThe volunteers alternate intake and record duties after each small group of returns. Both share the two tasks while keeping a clear current assignment."
    }
  ],
